;; How each first asking in reading\features-timeline.md connects to its feature,
;; one or two sentences each, written as the blog's own first person, read by
;; build.clj and shown under the quote on the timeline.
{"A universal language of prompting" "Here I was already asking for a language a model reads and writes in, with everything clearly labelled. That is what Smile grew into, a language of its own for prompting."
 "The prompt that explains itself" "I wanted a prompt that describes itself as it describes the task. Every Smile prompt now does this, its faces explaining what faces mean as they appear."
 "The section with a strong middle" "A dense middle with a clearly described top and bottom is a section. The faces of 2025 became that top and bottom."
 "The life of an instance" "Instances that learn over time and build their own context across many turns are the first sketch of what THE MAP now calls the life of an instance."
 "Smile games" "Learning to prompt as a game, fundamentals first, is the game of prompting that later became Smile games and SmileScape."
 "Test" "Metrics that read different things and can't all be maxed together are still how I test a prompt in Smile, with checks that each look at something else."
 "Lens" "Seeing how much attention each word receives was my first view into a model's tokens. It became the token lens, and then the lens over a whole library of prompts."
 "Pedagogy" "Scoring a prompt live while it's being typed is teaching made for one person from their own words, the pedagogy THE MAP names."
 "The Smile Sangha" "Separating roles so each can be learned on its own is the seed of a Sangha, agents with their own roles working as one."
 "The Prompt Doctor" "The De-GPT'er was the first prompt I offered as the Prompt Doctor, the face every prompt post is now told through."
 "Label" "Signalling a change in meaning with a mark or a code word is what a label does, the words between a header's faces that tell a model what a piece is."
 "Delimiter" "A string of emoji marking where a section starts is a delimiter. Two weeks later it became a single smiling face."
 "Version" "Sharing the first version on Discord began Smile's versions, v0.2, v0.3, v0.4, and later versions as definitions."
 "What Smile is for" "Maximum adoption, and animism giving prompters better outcomes, is the first time I said why Smile exists."
 "Offering" "Releasing the language for free, with teaching around it, is still how Smile is offered."
 "Prompt language and response language" "Asking for the reply in Markdown, with Smile kept inside code blocks, is where the language a prompt is written in and the language a response is written in first came apart."
 "Composition" "A syntax that lets all the modules play together by composing them is composition named, pieces gathered in an order into one prompt."
 "Sensing and Smile-ification" "Rewriting any prompt to be Smile compliant is Smile-ification, taking in an existing prompt and turning it into Smile."
 "Strict, Hybrid and Dense Smile" "Choosing single token faces to carry meaning cheaply is the token counting the three forms, Strict, Hybrid and Dense, were planned on. In July 2025 I wrote that no dense or strict Smile was developed yet."
 "Semantic Markdown" "Choosing Markdown to template the response is where Semantic Markdown, Smile's response format, began."
 "Integrity, the linter" "A linter in VS Code for people writing Smile is what the living linter became fifteen months later."
 "Raw text" "Raw text files that fill the editor when a document opens is raw text as THE MAP keeps it, the words stored apart from any composition that gathers them."
 "Transfer, one prompt across models" "Cross-compatible across all foundation models is transfer, one prompt carried from model to model."
 "Infrastructure" "A toolset of minification, parsing, variable replacement and conversion, all in one pipeline, is the infrastructure that carries Smile."
 "Synthetic data" "Token efficient instruction following data, readable at several levels, is the first idea of the synthetic data THE MAP later builds from exact algorithms."
 "Module" "Modules at section size and at writing size are the module itself, a reusable piece I could place wherever a prompt needed it."
 "Bringing in the best" "Naming PromptQuine as an existing answer for dense prompts was the first time Smile reached for work that already exists instead of building its own."
 "The editor" "A format an IDE could accept was my first wish for an editor that knows Smile. It became the Smile Composer, and then the editor THE MAP describes."
 "The two dimensions" "A more developed smile asking for more attention is importance, one of the two dimensions beside meta-information."
 "Linked compositions" "A file reference inside a prompt is the first linked composition, a prompt made of the files it points to."
 "Adjustment" "Amendments that change what a prompt asks for, such as bolding the important words, are adjustments, changes made from outside the prompt's text."
 "Run" "One prompt that sends an agent to get a thousand cowhides on an account is a run, a task carried out live by an agent."
 "Card" "A card telling an AI or a person how to use a prompt is the card every piece now carries."
 "Command" "Recording every manual use of a command, for everyone to see, is where my commands began, as things that are used and counted."
 "Conditions and actions" "If statements that models don't follow reliably are why conditions and actions moved outside the model, into Smile real time."
 "Master Header" "A short introduction at the top of every instruction, telling the model about Smile, is the Master Header, asked for here before it had a name."
 "Memory" "Keeping a model's thinking apart from its replies is the first act of memory, a record of what happened that can be read later."
 "Smile Chat, the surfaces I prompt in" "Giving the chat a window of its own was the first step of Smile Chat."
 "Recording" "Picking up what I posted into LM Studio from its log is the first recording, an exchange captured so Smile can read it."
 "The Temple" "Guru Rinpoche's presence moving through the apps by way of the Buddha eyes is the first sacred structure placed into Smile, the Temple."
 "Names, the figuration Smile grows into" "The ontological side of a name is why the parts of Smile are named with care, as figurations the system grows into. It is partly built, in how the prompt library is tagged."
 "THE MAP, the complete vision" "Registering everything in the map and building from it is the moment THE MAP became the centre of the work."
 "The work in hand" "Smile real time recognising the tasks I want done and the order they are done in is the work in hand, ordered and reordered as it runs."
 "Backtracking" "Ananda spoke of a method where a structure is made right where a habit already happens. Backtracking grew from it, returning to the work where it keeps recurring."
 "Arrival" "A message that waits until Claude has finished before it's received is the first arrival, a message given a time to land."
 "Composing from inside a prompt" "Editing the text of a composition and having it change the modules behind it is composing from inside a prompt."
 "Magnification" "Everything of one size in its own bucket, each tier going deeper, is magnification as THE MAP keeps it."
 "The dialogue suite" "Saying what you need kindly is the dialogue suite, kindness in the meaning and in letting the model do what's asked."
 "World" "Notes kept by location and loaded as I arrive somewhere is the first world, a game read by place."
 "The life of an instance, harvested" "The instance that learns over time, asked for in 2023, built at last as the harvest and inheritance every instance leaves."
 "All AI text written in Smile" "Every prompt converted into Smile before it runs, this decision is in these words."
 "Prompt Coach" "A coach that reads every prompt and offers each change for approval is the Prompt Coach, just as it was first described."
 "Place" "The shared refinement of a group's language as its individuation is Place, a community served by its own local AI. It is still to be built."
 "Prompt2SanghaEnergeticStructure" "Song lyrics restructured into 8 verses and a hub for Ganapati and the 8 Ganas is this operation in its first words."
 "SmileScape" "Progression tied to the account, with a playground where nothing is saved, is SmileScape as it was first described."}
